# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editorial Calendar — environment variables (all optional)
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in as needed. Vite only exposes
# variables prefixed with VITE_ to the client.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Demo (localStorage) admin credentials. Used only when Supabase is NOT
# configured. Change these before sharing a demo build.
VITE_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@digitalclick.com
VITE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=nexa2026
VITE_ADMIN_NAME=Administrador

# ── Production backend (Supabase) ──
# When VITE_SUPABASE_URL is set, wire up the Supabase adapter (see
# src/calendar-app/services/index.ts and supabaseService.ts.example).
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-KEY
